JAHS-Bench-201 query bridge memory (2026-09-15, measurement/resources.py, whole process tree)
Machine: i7-11800H, 31.7 GB RAM, Windows 11.

cifar10, random_search, 20 queries in one bridge:
  peak resident memory (loading the surrogate models): 17.47 GB
  resident memory after loading:                         1.85 GB
  first query (includes loading):                      ~224 s

Consequences for the parallel pipeline:
  * one bridge loads at a time: lock locks/jahs-bridge-load.lock
    (substrates/jahs_bench_201.py, P3NET_JAHS_LOAD_LOCK);
  * per JAHS worker after loading: ~1.9 GB bridge + 0.6-2.7 GB worker process;
  * 3 workers, worst case: 17.5 + 2 x 1.9 + 3 x 2.7 = ~29 GB of 31.7 GB
    -> plan default workers: 3.
